Subject: TEMP: point eyeo filter lists at the canonical ABP host

Not for shipping. This exists so the eyeo integration can be exercised
end to end while the e Foundation mirror is being set up.

cromite.org is unreachable (502s reported in uazo/cromite#2611 and
uazo/cromite#1845, and it is down again today), so every subscription
URL in the series currently resolves to nothing and no filter list can
be downloaded at all.

Base URL is now https://easylist-downloads.adblockplus.org/, which also
means the preloaded easylist/exceptionrules/anticv flatbuffers finally
match the subscription URLs, so filtering works on first launch before
anything is downloaded, and MaybeSplitCombinedAdblockList() now applies
because the host matches AdblockBaseFilterListUrl().

Default subscriptions changed while here:

 - removed badmojr/1Hosts: upstream retired the "Pro" tier (only Lite
   and Xtra remain), so the URL is dead wherever it is hosted, and a
   DNS blocklist is the wrong instrument for a browser content filter
 - removed Celenity/BadBlock Lite: written in uBO/AdGuard syntax, and
   UrlFilterOptions::FromString() discards an entire rule on an unknown
   option, so the ~40% of it that uses $important never loads
 - removed Cromite experimental filters: privileged, so it can run
   JavaScript in pages via snippet filters, hosted in a personal repo,
   and mostly a copy of abp-filters-anti-cv
 - EasyPrivacy now subscribes at first run. It was off, which meant a
   de-Googled browser shipped ad blocking without tracker blocking
 - Fanboy's Notifications Blocking List now subscribes at first run

Leaves four first-run lists (EasyList, EasyPrivacy, ABP filters,
Fanboy's Notifications) plus the 25 locale-matched regional lists,
all from one maintained publisher in native ABP syntax. ABP filters
stays privileged; nothing else does except the local user filters.

Before shipping: repoint GetHost() at the e Foundation mirror, and
decide whether the anti-circumvention list keeps privileged status.
